// The std.unicode package. Each module owns its declarations and their
// English names: an alias can only name a declaration of its own module, and
// an import brings in only the imported module's own public names, so this
// file cannot re-export the others. Import the whole package selectively,
// `from std.unicode import unicode_category_of, is_unicode_scalar;`, or one
// module, `import std.unicode.general_category;`. The nested data and
// algorithms directories are separate packages.
